# W-0043 / P7-1. Build context for the .NET images (repository root).
#
# The point is not only speed: anything listed here cannot end up in a layer by accident, so the
# ignore file is also the first line against a secret or a local artifact being baked into an
# image (D-05).

# Build output — stale bin/obj from a host build would be copied over the container's own.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/.vs/
**/TestResults/

# Not needed to publish api or worker.
admin-ui/
tests/
docs/
specs/
plan/
prompt/
seed/
deploy/observability/
deploy/chaos/
.gitnexus/
.claude/

# Repository and tooling metadata.
.git/
.github/
.gitlab/
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules/
**/*.md
!README.md

# Local environment files. None are needed to build, and every one of them is a way for a
# developer's credentials to reach a registry.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pfx
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# W-0122 builds only the preset ONNX runtime. Reference samples, cloning/training apps, web UI,
# upstream deployment files and tests remain vendored for provenance but cannot enter image layers.
third_party/vieneu-tts/apps/
third_party/vieneu-tts/client/
third_party/vieneu-tts/docker/
third_party/vieneu-tts/examples/
third_party/vieneu-tts/finetune/
third_party/vieneu-tts/tests/
third_party/vieneu-tts/src/vieneu/assets/samples/
